return {h=3,w=54,cr=190,hc=20,bh=70,gr="medium",eg={"bug","plant"},st={35,70,55,45,55,25},ab={{27,0},{87,0},{6,1}},genus={en="Mushroom Pokémon",es="Pokémon Hongo",pt="Pokémon Cogumelo"},flavor={en={[1]="Burrows to suck tree roots. The mushrooms on its back grow by drawing nutrients from the bug host.",[2]="Burrows to suck tree roots. The mushrooms on its back grow by drawing nutrients from the bug host.",[3]="Burrows under the ground to gnaw on tree roots. The mushrooms on its back absorb most of the nutrition.",[4]="It is doused with mushroom spores when it is born. As its body grows, mushrooms sprout from its back.",[5]="As its body grows large, oriental mushrooms named tochukaso start sprouting out of its back.",[6]="The tochukaso growing on this Pokémon's back orders it to extract juice from tree trunks.",[7]="PARAS has parasitic mushrooms growing on its back called tochukaso. They grow large by drawing nutrients from the BUG Pokémon host. They are highly valued as a medicine for extending life.",[8]="PARAS has parasitic mushrooms growing on its back called tochukaso. They grow large by drawing nutrients from this BUG Pokémon host. They are highly valued as a medicine for extending life.",[9]="A PARAS has parasitic tochukaso mushrooms growing on its back. They grow by drawing nutrients from the host. They are valued as a medicine for long life.",[10]="Growing out of the bug’s back are mushrooms called tochukaso. The mushrooms grow with the bug host.",[11]="Burrows to suck tree roots. The mushrooms on its back grow by drawing nutrients from the bug host.",[12]="Mushrooms named tochukaso grow on its back. They grow along with the host PARAS.",[13]="Mushrooms named tochukaso grow on its back. They grow along with the host PARAS.",[14]="Mushrooms named tochukaso grow on its back. They grow along with the host PARAS.",[15]="It is doused with mushroom spores when it is born. As its body grows, mushrooms sprout from its back.",[16]="As its body grows, large mushrooms named tochukaso start sprouting out of its back.",[17]="Mushrooms named tochukaso grow on its back. They grow along with the host Paras.",[18]="Mushrooms named tochukaso grow on its back. They grow along with the host Paras.",[21]="Mushrooms named tochukaso grow on its back. They grow along with the host Paras.",[22]="Mushrooms named tochukaso grow on its back. They grow along with the host Paras.",[23]="Growing out of the bug’s back are mushrooms called tochukaso. The mushrooms grow with the bug host.",[24]="Burrows under the ground to gnaw on tree roots. The mushrooms on its back absorb most of the nutrition.",[25]="Paras has parasitic mushrooms growing on its back called tochukaso. They grow large by drawing nutrients from this Bug Pokémon host. They are highly valued as a medicine for extending life.",[26]="Paras has parasitic mushrooms growing on its back called tochukaso. They grow large by drawing nutrients from this Bug Pokémon host. They are highly valued as a medicine for extending life.",[27]="No matter how much it eats, the mushrooms growing on its back steal away most of the nutrients it consumes.",[28]="Mushrooms called tochukaso sprout from its back. They can be dried and powdered to make a medicine used to extend life.",[29]="Whether it’s due to a lack of moisture or a lack of nutrients, in Alola the mushrooms on Paras don’t grow up quite right.",[30]="The mushrooms, known as tochukaso, are controlling the bug. Even if the bug bugs the mushrooms, they tell it to bug off.",[31]="Burrows under the ground to gnaw on tree roots. The mushrooms on its back absorb most of the nutrition.",[32]="Burrows under the ground to gnaw on tree roots. The mushrooms on its back absorb most of the nutrition.",[39]="Sometimes seen at the foot of trees in humid forests. The mushrooms on its back, called tochukaso, are not present on infant specimens and instead emerge as Paras matures."},es={[23]="Lleva en el lomo dos setas parásitas llamadas tochukaso, que crecen con él."